# Tests — EXP-POL E-6 submission and time limits

Assertion-based tests for `ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible`. E-6 is a 60/120-day
staircase, and a staircase is exactly the shape that an off-by-one hides in, so
every step is pinned on both sides: 59, 60, 61, 119, 120 and 121 days, each with
and without the line manager's certification.

The expense is incurred on 2025-01-01 throughout, so the submission dates read
directly as elapsed days: 2025-03-01 is day 59, 2025-03-02 is day 60,
2025-03-03 is day 61, 2025-04-30 is day 119, 2025-05-01 is day 120 and
2025-05-02 is day 121.

`delay_certified_for_good_reason` is the judgement input. Every test supplies it
explicitly, and the pairs of tests at days 61, 119 and 120 differ in nothing
else — which is what demonstrates that the module is deciding on the
certification and not on the length of the delay.

Counterexamples found by the adversarial reviewer are kept separately, in
`tests/counterexamples/`, and are re-run by `scripts/check.sh`.

> Using ClaimWindow

## E6_1_SameDay

Zero days elapsed: well within E-6.1.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_SameDay:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_SameDay:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 0
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_1_Day59

Day 59, no certification needed.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_Day59:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_Day59:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-03-01|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 59
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_1_Day60

Boundary, admitted side: "within 60 days" includes day 60.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_Day60:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_Day60:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-03-02|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 60
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_1_Day60WithCertification

Day 60 needs no certification, and having one changes nothing.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_Day60WithCertification:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_Day60WithCertification:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-03-02|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 60
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_1_Day61Uncertified

Boundary, refused side: day 61 is outside E-6.1 and E-6.2 is not engaged
without the certification.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_Day61Uncertified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_Day61Uncertified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-03-03|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 61
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_2_Day61Certified

E-6.2, first day on which it can bite: day 61 with the certification.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_2_Day61Certified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_2_Day61Certified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-03-03|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 61
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_2_Day119Certified

Mid-window, certified.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_2_Day119Certified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_2_Day119Certified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-04-30|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 119
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_2_Day119Uncertified

Mid-window, uncertified: E-6.1 governs and the claim is out of time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_2_Day119Uncertified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_2_Day119Uncertified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-04-30|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 119
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_2_Day120Certified

Boundary, admitted side: "within 120 days" includes day 120.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_2_Day120Certified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_2_Day120Certified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-05-01|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 120
  assertion r.admissible = true
```

## E6_2_Day120Uncertified

Day 120 without the certification is still out of time under E-6.1.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_2_Day120Uncertified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_2_Day120Uncertified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-05-01|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 120
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_3_Day121Certified

Boundary, refused side, and the point of E-6.3: day 121 is refused "in any
circumstances", so the certification does not save it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_3_Day121Certified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_3_Day121Certified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-05-02|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 121
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_3_Day121Uncertified

Day 121 uncertified.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_3_Day121Uncertified:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_3_Day121Uncertified:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-05-02|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 121
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_3_LongStopWellBeyond120Days

Day 200 with a certification: the long-stop is absolute.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_3_LongStopWellBeyond120Days:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_3_LongStopWellBeyond120Days:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2025-01-01|
      -- submission_date: |2025-07-20|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: true
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 200
  assertion r.admissible = false
```

## E6_1_AcrossALeapDay

The elapsed period is a count of calendar days, so a leap day counts as a day:
2024-02-01 to 2024-04-01 is 60 days because February 2024 had 29.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE6_1_AcrossALeapDay:
  output r content ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible

scope TestE6_1_AcrossALeapDay:
  definition r equals
    output of ClaimWindow.ClaimAdmissible with {
      -- expense_incurred_date: |2024-02-01|
      -- submission_date: |2024-04-01|
      -- delay_certified_for_good_reason: false
    }
  assertion r.days_elapsed = 60
  assertion r.admissible = true
```
